DISPOSITION

The engineering is good and I want that recorded plainly. Both defects this
opus was failed for are properly fixed — the right containment relation in the
right place, the reopen edge that lets a failed review say so without
stranding the work — and I verified each by driving it, not by reading the
diff. `red` still refuses to record a passing command, which remains the best
thing in this opus. verify and `npm test` agree. 879 green. `check` is at zero
blocking with the opus still in the rule's line of sight, which is what round 3
asked for and did not get.

It does not close, because nine of its twelve behaviours cannot show their own
red, and this cascade already decided one round ago that that is blocking. I
will not hold W-021 to a standard and sign W-020 past it on the same day.

W-020 stays in `building`. Round 5 is nine reds and a kept script.

